There's a clean extension point: the `AutoFixer` interface pattern. I'll add a `RuntimeLogger` interface:

```go
// RuntimeLogger — необязательный интерфейс агента: хвост логов рантайма,
// накопленный инструментом ReadAppLogs (Ф-2). Раннер после раунда подмешивает
// его модели СКРЫТЫМ промптом — так же, как диагностики LSP.
type RuntimeLogger interface {
    // TakeAppLogTail забирает и очищает накопленные строки логов рантайма.
    TakeAppLogTail() (source string, lines []string)
}
```

`FileOps` already has `TakeAppLogTail() (string, []string)` — signature matches! So `*tools.FileOps` automatically satisfies it.

Then in the runner loop, after the autofix block, add the app-log feed. The runner must check `agent.(RuntimeLogger)`. But the agent passed to Generate is the `agents.Agent` (e.g. `*developer.BackendDeveloper`), not `*tools.FileOps`. The AutoFixer check works because the agent types embed `*base` with FileOps... Let me check: `agents/developer` — does it implement `TakeTouched` and `LspCheckFiles` by embedding FileOps? It embeds `base` which has `FileOps *tools.FileOps` as a named field, not embedded... Let me check how AutoFixer is satisfied.

